  "2016 P2 Q10": {"v":"indices.negative-power-pre2022p1","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(n^6\\)",null,null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"Which rule of indices deals with the bracket, and which with the multiplication?","step":"Start with \\((n^2)^3\\): a power of a power means multiply the powers.","watch":"Adding a negative power makes the total smaller: here it is below zero. Then write it as a positive power on the bottom of a fraction."},
  "2016 P2 Q11": {"v":"similarity.area-from-cost","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\frac{60}{100}\\)","\\(13.75 \\times (\\frac{60}{100})^2\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"The pictures are similar, and the cost goes with the area. If lengths scale by a factor, what happens to areas?","step":"Find the scale factor from the large picture to the small one using the widths. It should be less than \\(1\\).","watch":"Area, and so the cost, uses the scale factor squared. Give the cost in pounds and pence."},
