  "2019 P1 Q9": {"v":"quadratics.parabola-maximum","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":[null,null,null],"marksLine":"2 marks, (i) 1 mark","nudge":"The axis of symmetry passes through the turning point. In \\(y = b - (x + a)^2\\), what are the coordinates of the turning point?","step":"The axis of symmetry is the vertical line through the maximum turning point.","watch":"Write the axis as an equation, \\(x = \\dots\\), not a number on its own. In (b), the sign flips for \\(a\\) but not for \\(b\\)."},
  "2019 P1 Q10": {"v":"vectors.components-midpoint","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":[null,"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{PR} + \\overrightarrow{RQ}\\) OR \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 8 \\end{pmatrix}\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"Which route from P to Q uses vectors you know? In (b), how far along PR is M?","step":"For (a), go from P to R and then from R to Q: add the two column vectors.","watch":"In (b), M is halfway along PR: use half of a vector you already know."},
