  "2025 P2 Q12": {"v":"bearings.two-sides","marks":[1,1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\frac{\\sin C}{250} = \\frac{\\sin 41}{200}\\)","\\(\\sin C = \\frac{250 \\times \\sin 41}{200} (= 0.820...)\\)","\\(55(.09...)\\)",null],"marksLine":"4 marks","nudge":"Which angle inside triangle ABC can the bearing \\(131^\\circ\\) give you? Which rule links it to the sides you know?","step":"At A, east is \\(90^\\circ\\) round from north: take \\(90^\\circ\\) from the bearing to get angle BAC.","watch":"The sine rule gives angle C first. Find angle ABC from the angle sum, then turn it into a bearing measured from north at B."},
