  "2026 P1 Q1": {"v":"expanding.binomial-trinomial","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(y^3 - 3y^2 + 2y \\dots\\)","\\(y^3 - 3y^2 + 2y + 4y^2 - 12y + 8\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"Every term in the first bracket multiplies every term in the second. How many products should you have before you collect like terms?","step":"Multiply each of \\(y^2\\), \\(-3y\\) and \\(2\\) by \\(y\\), then each by \\(4\\): six products in all.","watch":"Keep each sign with its term when you collect like terms: there are negatives to combine."},
  "2026 P1 Q2": {"v":"percentages.part-of-whole","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(60\\% = 180\\)","\\((10\\% =) \\frac{180}{6}\\) or \\((1\\% =) \\frac{180}{60}\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"180 miles is \\(60\\%\\) of the full distance. How could you get from \\(60\\%\\) to \\(100\\%\\)?","step":"Write \\(60\\% = 180\\) miles, then work out what \\(1\\%\\) (or \\(10\\%\\)) of the full distance is.","watch":"180 is \\(60\\%\\) of the answer, not the amount to take \\(60\\%\\) of."},
