  "2026 P1 Q6": {"v":"straight-line.best-fit","marks":[1,1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\frac{40}{60}\\)","\\(y - 54 = \\frac{40}{60}(x - 30)\\) or \\(y - 94 = \\frac{40}{60}(x - 90)\\)","\\(F = \\frac{2}{3}P + 34\\) or \\(3F = 2P + 102\\)",null],"marksLine":"4 marks","nudge":"A straight line needs a gradient and a starting point. How can points A and B give you both?","step":"Use A\\((30, 54)\\) and B\\((90, 94)\\): the gradient is the change in \\(F\\) divided by the change in \\(P\\).","watch":"The gradient is the change in \\(F\\) over the change in \\(P\\), not the other way up."},
