  "2026 P1 Q14": {"v":"factorising.solve-non-unitary","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\((5x \\dots 2)(2x \\dots 3)\\) or \\(5x(2x + 3) - 2(2x + 3)\\) or \\(2x(5x - 2) + 3(5x - 2)\\)","\\((5x - 2)(2x + 3)\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"The question says factorise. What two brackets multiply to give \\(10x^2 + 11x - 6\\)?","step":"\\(10x^2\\) could be \\(10x \\times x\\) or \\(5x \\times 2x\\), and \\(-6\\) needs factors with opposite signs. Try pairs until the middle term is \\(+11x\\).","watch":"Use factorising, not the quadratic formula: the question sets the method, and the formula scores nothing."},
