  "2026 P2 Q3": {"v":"similarity.volume-scale-down","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\frac{8}{12}\\ (= 0 \\cdot 66\\dots)\\)","\\(\\left(\\frac{8}{12}\\right)^3 \\times 540\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"The bottles are similar. If the lengths scale by a factor, what happens to the volumes?","step":"Find the scale factor from the larger bottle to the tester using the heights. It should be less than \\(1\\).","watch":"Volume uses the scale factor cubed, not squared or on its own. The tester must hold less than 540 ml."},
  "2026 P2 Q4": {"v":"simeq.construct-combine","marks":[1,1,3,1],"shows":[null,null,"\\(10c + 12p = 90\\) and \\(21c + 12p = 156\\); or \\(35c + 42p = 315\\) and \\(35c + 20p = 260\\); or \\(20c + 24p = 180\\) and \\(42c + 24p = 312\\)",null],"marksLine":"6 marks","nudge":"Each sentence gives you one equation. Once you know \\(c\\) and \\(p\\), what does (c) ask for?","step":"Write the time for the cups plus the time for the plates, and set it equal to the total time.","watch":"Solve algebraically, not by trying numbers, and do not stop at \\(c\\) and \\(p\\): (c) wants the time for 10 cups and 8 plates."},
  "2026 P2 Q5": {"v":"pythagoras.chord-radius","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["a right-angled triangle with \\(12 \\cdot 5\\) and \\(9\\) marked and the right angle shown","\\(12 \\cdot 5^2 + 9^2\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"What do you know about a line from the centre to the midpoint of a chord? What shape does it make with a radius?","step":"Join O to A to make the right-angled triangle OBA. AB is half the chord.","watch":"The radius OA is the hypotenuse, so add the squares. Use half of 25, not 25."},
