  "2026 P2 Q7": {"v":"pythagoras.converse-sides","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(88^2 + 105^2\\) and \\(137^2\\)","\\(88^2 + 105^2 = 18769\\) **and** \\(137^2 = 18769\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"If the triangle were right-angled, which side would be the hypotenuse, and what would be true?","step":"Take the longest side as the one that would be the hypotenuse. Work out the two shorter sides squared and added, and the longest squared, each on its own.","watch":"Do not start by writing \\(88^2 + 105^2 = 137^2\\): that assumes what you are testing. Work out each side, then compare them and name the converse of Pythagoras."},
