  "2026 P2 Q9": {"v":"alg-fractions.divide-squares-on-top","marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\frac{x^2 - 81}{5} \\times \\frac{2}{x + 9}\\)","\\(\\frac{(x - 9)(x + 9)}{\\dots} \\dots\\)",null],"marksLine":"3 marks","nudge":"How do you divide by a fraction? Can the top, \\(x^2 - 81\\), be factorised?","step":"Turn the division into a multiplication by turning the second fraction upside down.","watch":"Factorise \\(x^2 - 81\\) as a difference of two squares before you cancel: you can cancel whole factors only, not terms."},
  "2026 P2 Q10": {"v":"sector.polygon-segment","marks":[1,1,1,2],"shows":["\\(72\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 11 \\times 11 \\times \\sin 72\\ (= 57 \\cdot 5\\dots)\\)","\\(\\frac{72}{360} \\times \\pi \\times 11^2\\) **or** \\(\\frac{1}{5} \\times \\pi \\times 11^2\\ (= 76 \\cdot 0\\dots)\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\pi r^2 - \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\)"],"marksLine":"5 marks","nudge":"A segment is a sector with a triangle taken away. What is the angle at the centre for one side of the pentagon?","step":"The five vertices split the circle into five equal sectors. Find the angle at O for one of them.","watch":"Take the triangle from one sector, not from the whole circle, and find the triangle's area with \\(\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\)."},
